{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1180876-mikhaili-alternative-death-theory","id":1180876,"title":"Mikhaili- Alternative Death Theory","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-30T13:58:22-08:00","id":1180876,"title":"Mikhaili- Alternative Death Theory","content":"For those who missed it, in Half Damned we are presented with a new, Lost Clan- the Mikhaili, the Winter Kings of ancient Siberia. According to book, the most common theory among the Kindred about the clan's death tells that once, the Mikhailli were few in numbers as they ruled in cold wasteland. However, as the Gangrel came from the west in large, numbers, the Mikhailli were overwhelmed and started to Embrace en masses. As they did, their once potent blood as grew thin, and eventually they had no power in it, spawning nothing but revenants. Seeing the error of their ways, they have started to diableriez their own kin, yet it was too late, and only a single member of the clan has survived and gained a pale shadow of their old power, and went to establish a new clan of its own. The Gangrel slaughtered those Mikhailli which survived, and the clan was no more.<br /> <br /> That's, of course, probably a lie.<br /> <br /> The Blood doesn't work that way. You can't just Embrace so many times that it runs out. Instead, it propagate, expand, grows stronger and weaker with the passage of time. Even the book states it, and mentions that it probably is nothing more than a twisting of history, a cautionary tale about the consequences of Embracing without control and the creation of numerous revenants. However, the Mikhailli did existed, once, and something did killed them, destroying the source of their power and bringing them to a state nothing but revenant came from their suddenly so thin, thin blood.<br /> <br /> Something like VII.<br /> <br /> Among the three presented options for VII in their core book, one seems way too.. familar, when you connect the dots- that is, the Betrayed. Taking place in the ancient Eastern Europe-Northern Asia region (which is the place of origin for the Mikhailli), the King of Day has made a pact with the Prince of Night, giving the vampire and its kin solace while the king and his kin gained access to the vampire's Vitae and its blessings. As long as the Prince was active, the compact was kept- but as he fell to torpor, the one to replace him didn't had the same respect to the king. As the number of the king's kin grew, the toil upon the vampires grew as well- more vampires were needed, and more blood was demanded. Eventually, the vampires killed a peasant, breaking the compact. The king killed one of them in return, to show the vampire who holds the reigns. The vampire, with his anger, slaughtered seven of the king's daughters, and let him to die out as the Vitae was consumed in his body and the month was in due. In his despair, the king clawed his way to the old Prince's coffin, devouring his heart and soul in order to gain the so desired life. The outcome, however, was unexpected- for he did not became a ghoul. Instead, he and his seven children became vampires, and they took an oath to avenge their family and destroy each and every last vampire on earth.<br /> <br /> That's probably a lie, too.<br /> <br /> I mean, again, the story doesn't make sense- humans can't resist the bonds of blood generated by Vitae, and they can't commit diablerie upon vampires. However, again, what we need to do is to connect the dots- we have a vampire, which is said to escape Rome (making him a potential Julli), but we can't really take it as validated truth. What we do know is that this vampire has escaped something, to some ancient kingdom ruled by a king. The king and the vampire has probably made some kind of a pact, which was eventually broken, as expected. The massacre of the daughters has undoubtedly happened, as the ghosts are still around. If we connect the dots, we could get the following picture- that somewhere in the past, the Gangrel has invaded the homeland of the Mikhailli, and started to slaughter them all. One of their kind escaped to the king's realm, and made with him the Compact, allowing him to procreate and establish his clan anew. When the compact broke, the king probably didn't devoured the literal heart of the vampire, but somehow, as a paert of the massacre, the ghosts has managed to steal the power behind the Mikhailli's creation and grant it to the king, which has later Embraced his children to create the Seven Houses of the Betrayed. How exactly it happened and what that power was I don't really know, but as it happened the Mikhailli has lost their ability to Embrace. They could create only revenants, and as such, became lost.<br /> <br /> So- what do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T05:58:41-08:00","id":1182566,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a pretty good arrangement of events - it has been quite some time since i last read VII, but even though the image is far from complete, the dots seem to connect nicely indeed.<br /> It's interesting for certain to see some of the other takes of VII getting a callback after so many years with the Akhud getting all the love. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T06:13:16-08:00","id":1182569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1180876-mikhaili-alternative-death-theory?p=1182566#post1182566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a pretty good arrangement of events - it has been quite some time since i last read VII, but even though the image is far from complete, the dots seem to connect nicely indeed.<br /> It's interesting for certain to see some of the other takes of VII getting a callback after so many years with the Akhud getting all the love. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>yeah- actually, the Betrayed are my favorite VII version, but I also like the Akhud, which is why I've adapted them into a &quot;non VII version&quot; (still need to finish working on the &quot;non VII&quot; version of the Covenant...). Every once and awhile, however, I play with the concept of having &quot;seven different VII&quot;, but I need to see how I could justify it beyond &quot;the ST said so&quot; :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T08:12:02-08:00","id":1182604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1180876-mikhaili-alternative-death-theory?p=1182569#post1182569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah- actually, the Betrayed are my favorite VII version, but I also like the Akhud, which is why I've adapted them into a &quot;non VII version&quot; (still need to finish working on the &quot;non VII&quot; version of the Covenant...). Every once and awhile, however, I play with the concept of having &quot;seven different VII&quot;, but I need to see how I could justify it beyond &quot;the ST said so&quot; :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's something like a non-VII version of the Akhud in the books - or maybe i'm misinterpreting something of the lost clans stuff in 2nd edition books like that - either way, certainly worth looking out for, i think.<br /> <br /> Seven versions of VII existed could be based on something as simple as some force with an interest on (messing up with) the kindred working to maintain that many lines of action/conspiracies/cults going or out of some esoteric urge/limitation/resource it works with. Individual heads of the monster may come and go, but seven brands always stay active on some level or another. Just an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}